While it's true that animations using the -webkit-animation property are not supported in modern browsers (like Chrome and Firefox), to verify compatibility with Safari 9 specifically, you can use the following CSS:

```css
@-webkit-keyframes loading {
  0% {
    background: #f1f1f1;
  }
  50% {
    background: #4CAF50;
  }
  100% {
    background: #f1f1f1;
  }
}

@-webkit-keyframes spinning {
  0% { transform: rotate(0deg); }
  100% { transform: rotate(360deg); }
}

@-webkit-animation loading 2s linear both forwards;
@-webkit-animation spinning 2s linear both;
```

